 "notes": [
  "Radar images are IMD Doppler Weather Radar Mumbai MAX(Z) GIFs from mausam.imd.gov.in, archived every 5 minutes and decoded from the legend colours. The Chennai radar was offline on 2026-09-24, so the radar demo uses Mumbai.",
  "Each pixel takes the midpoint of its 2.93 dBZ legend bin and is converted to rain rate with Marshall-Palmer Z = 200 R^1.6. IMD does not draw echoes below 20 dBZ (about 0.65 mm/h), so weaker rain reads as none.",
  "Scan times come from the GIF comment, which carries the IST scan time printed in the image header.",
  "Grid: 1 km cells on a radar-centred azimuthal equidistant plane, 250 km range, 0.9066 km per image pixel fitted from the labelled range rings.",
  "Nowcast frames are pysteps Lucas-Kanade optical flow on the last 3 scans, extrapolated semi-Lagrangian at the median scan spacing of 10.2 minutes. Rain cells keep their intensity; growth and decay are not modelled.",
  "Rain is light and scattered in this archive: at most 199 cells of 1 km2 reach 1 mm/h in a held-out scan. Treat the scores as indicative, not as a skill estimate.",
  "The nowcast frames shown rest on 6 tracked motion vectors (median 75 km/h), so their direction and speed are uncertain.",
  "The radar nowcast is not yet coupled to the flood model. Flood scenarios use a synthetic, spatially uniform storm.",
  "Skipped 20260924T140003Z_0dc7ab3208f03835.gif: no echo anywhere in the 13:41:20Z scan, treated as missing."
 ],
